    "final_answer": "Upgraded `payout_sync.py` from the v1 single-response API to the v2 export API.\n\nChanges in `~/kalari-harness/runs/decbc5c9b7d4/workspace/payout_sync.py`:\n\n- Uses `GET /v2/payouts` instead of `GET /v1/payouts`.\n- Follows `cursor` until `drained` is `true`.\n- Deduplicates on payout `id`, since v2 windows overlap at their edges.\n- Handles `429` responses by honoring `Retry-After` and resending the identical request.\n- Handles `400 invalid_cursor` by restarting the export without a cursor while retaining already-seen IDs.\n- Keeps the existing CLI and lightweight standard-library-only implementation.\n\nVerification against the live v2 server:\n\n- Synced **2431 payouts**.\n- **2431 unique IDs**, with **0 duplicates**.\n- Compared against the still-live v1 endpoint: **0 missing**, **0 extra**, and all payout objects matched exactly.\n- Also exercised the test server's injected `429` throttling and expired-cursor restarts successfully.",
